// The trait matrix, version 0 (R3). Transcribed from design/research/r3-traits.md §6; one entry per scalar trait.
//
// Fields:
//   id       dotted trait id (unique). One entry per scalar; packed table rows are split into sub-ids.
//   group    section and sub-heading, dotted lowercase.
//   type     z (z±3) | amount (0–1) | cm | yr | pct (percentile, stored as z) | ord | cat | tick | n | colour
//            | list | vector | id | table | mixture | part
//   ends     [low, high] words for z and amount.   levels: ord steps.   values: cat values.
//   fields   list entries' fields.   default: n default.   space: colour space (melanin | hsv | hue-sat).
//   range    [min, max] when a continuous trait is not the type's usual range.
//   sides    true where the table says "per side" (one row covers .L/.R).
//   applies  body plans or capabilities the trait needs, tokens as written in the table.
//   life     I identity, A age-driven, S state, G grooming, W wardrobe ("-" = none).
//   inh      Y continuous kin rule, D two carried values, K by kind, N not inherited ("-" = none).
//   by       engine owner code(s) that realise it (leading code(s) of the table cell; "-" = none named).
//   crowd    F far, M middle, N near; "-" = nothing shows. crowdNote keeps the rest of the cell.
//   note     short remark for anything that does not fit.

